WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:02.652
"Hey, Henry!

2
00:00:02.713 --> 00:00:03.653
Come out here!"

3
00:00:04.194 --> 00:00:10.419
Henry looked out the window and saw his cousin waving at him from the sidewalk in front of

4
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:12.380
his house.

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.862
Maggie was nine years old and lived next door.

6
00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:17.504
Her mom and Henry's mom were sisters.

7
00:00:32.444 --> 00:00:33.485
"What do you want?"

8
00:00:34.205 --> 00:00:35.786
Henry called down to Maggie.

9
00:00:35.806 --> 00:00:37.448
"I'm busy."

10
00:00:38.048 --> 00:00:39.489
He glanced at his computer.

11
00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:45.493
He'd just finished lunch, and now he was playing his favorite game, Puzzle Pirates.

12
00:00:46.474 --> 00:00:50.497
All he had to do was solve one more puzzle, and he would reach Level Ten.

13
00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.458
"Just come down here!"

14
00:00:53.138 --> 00:00:54.019
Maggie yelled again.

15
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:55.680
Henry sighed.

16
00:00:56.561 --> 00:01:00.844
He was two years older than Maggie, but that didn't stop her from bossing him around.

17
00:01:02.112 --> 00:01:05.554
His best friend, Cole, always told him that he should just ignore her.

18
00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:10.196
But Maggie was usually so loud and dramatic, she was hard to ignore!

19
00:01:11.497 --> 00:01:14.299
Henry turned off his computer and headed outside.

20
00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:19.361
Maggie was waiting for him and holding a handmade cardboard sign.

21
00:01:19.381 --> 00:01:22.723
"Look at this," she said.

22
00:01:22.743 --> 00:01:24.624
"Isn't it awesome?"

23
00:01:25.665 --> 00:01:36.690
The sign read: MAGGIE'S LEMONADE STAND ONE CUP: 25 cents TWO CUPS: 45 cents BELLTOWN'S BEST BEVERAGE!

24
00:01:38.091 --> 00:01:39.671
Maggie was very artistic.

25
00:01:40.472 --> 00:01:42.973
She'd drawn a glass of lemonade below the words.

26
00:01:43.993 --> 00:01:46.754
It looked so realistic that it made Henry thirsty.

27
00:01:46.774 --> 00:01:49.895
"Great sign," Henry said.

28
00:01:49.915 --> 00:01:51.956
"Maybe I'll buy a cup."

29
00:01:51.976 --> 00:01:55.158
"You won't have to," Maggie said.

30
00:01:55.178 --> 00:01:57.639
"You'll get your lemonade for free."

31
00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:00.580
Henry was instantly suspicious.

32
00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:06.972
If Maggie was running a lemonade stand to make money, why would she give away the lemonade for

33
00:02:07.052 --> 00:02:09.254
free? "What do you mean?"

34
00:02:09.835 --> 00:02:10.435
he asked.

35
00:02:11.136 --> 00:02:11.756
She grinned.

36
00:02:11.776 --> 00:02:16.200
"You'll get it for free because you're an employee," she said.

37
00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.063
"I hereby hire you to help me with my lemonade stand."

38
00:02:20.643 --> 00:02:22.005
Henry rolled his eyes.

39
00:02:22.025 --> 00:02:24.667
"Are you kidding me?"

40
00:02:25.107 --> 00:02:25.628
he said.

41
00:02:25.648 --> 00:02:28.810
"Lemonade stands are for babies."

42
00:02:29.811 --> 00:02:30.772
Maggie scowled.

43
00:02:31.544 --> 00:02:32.685
"No, they're not!"

44
00:02:32.705 --> 00:02:36.047
"Yes, they are," Henry said.

45
00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:39.409
"Why do you want to do something like that anyway?"

46
00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:47.255
"Mom and Dad said I can take horseback-riding lessons if I pay half of the cost myself," Maggie

47
00:02:47.315 --> 00:02:53.259
explained. "I figured I could make lots of money selling lemonade while it's hot out.

48
00:02:53.919 --> 00:02:56.761
I'll switch to hot chocolate when the weather turns cold."

49
00:02:57.641 --> 00:02:59.903
"Sounds like a good plan," Henry said.

50
00:02:59.923 --> 00:03:01.344
"So you'll help?"

51
00:03:02.004 --> 00:03:03.085
Maggie looked excited.

52
00:03:03.105 --> 00:03:05.486
"Nope," Henry said.

53
00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.948
Maggie tried to change his mind.

54
00:03:09.369 --> 00:03:11.791
She promised him all the free lemonade he could drink.

55
00:03:12.751 --> 00:03:15.593
Then she told him he could have 10 percent of the profits.

56
00:03:16.594 --> 00:03:18.075
Henry just shook his head.

57
00:03:18.095 --> 00:03:20.416
"No, thanks," he said.

58
00:03:20.436 --> 00:03:22.518
"Good luck with your new business.

59
00:03:23.498 --> 00:03:24.499
I'm going to Cole's."

60
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.601
He walked over to Cole's house on the next block.

61
00:03:28.462 --> 00:03:31.344
The two of them played soccer for a while in Cole's yard.

62
00:03:32.608 --> 00:03:35.370
Then they headed back to Henry's house to play Puzzle Pirates.

63
00:03:36.631 --> 00:03:38.913
On the way they passed Maggie's lemonade stand.

64
00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:43.316
The stand was a table set up on the sidewalk in front of Maggie's house.

65
00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:48.020
Two teenage girls were standing nearby sipping lemonade from paper cups.

66
00:03:49.121 --> 00:03:51.623
A boy with a skateboard was chugging his lemonade.

67
00:03:53.084 --> 00:03:57.287
A little boy clung to his mother's hand while she leaned against the table and talked on her

68
00:03:57.327 --> 00:03:57.888
cell phone.

69
00:03:58.784 --> 00:04:03.288
Maggie was nearby chatting with a kid named Nathan and his little sister, Nora.

70
00:04:04.088 --> 00:04:08.032
It looked as if Nathan and Nora had just returned from the local swimming pool.

71
00:04:08.752 --> 00:04:10.434
Their bathing suits were still wet.

72
00:04:11.354 --> 00:04:14.917
When Maggie spotted Henry and Cole coming, she hurried to meet them.

73
00:04:14.937 --> 00:04:16.659
"Want some lemonade?"

74
00:04:17.159 --> 00:04:17.659
she asked.

75
00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.901
"It's a dollar per cup."

76
00:04:20.842 --> 00:04:21.763
"A dollar?"

77
00:04:22.263 --> 00:04:22.904
Henry said.

78
00:04:22.924 --> 00:04:25.546
"I thought you were charging 25 cents."

79
00:04:25.586 --> 00:04:29.556
"Yeah!" Cole pointed to the sign.

80
00:04:29.576 --> 00:04:31.417
"It's written right there.

81
00:04:31.797 --> 00:04:34.538
See?" Maggie tossed her head.

82
00:04:34.558 --> 00:04:37.479
"That's the price for normal people.

83
00:04:38.639 --> 00:04:41.740
Rotten cousins and their friends get charged extra."

84
00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:47.141
"Fine. I wasn't thirsty anyway," Henry said, rolling his eyes.

85
00:04:47.161 --> 00:04:49.062
"Come on, Cole.

86
00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.803
We have plenty of soda at my house."

87
00:04:52.803 --> 00:04:54.203
They started to walk away.

88
00:04:55.043 --> 00:04:56.464
But Maggie ran after them.

89
00:04:59.084 --> 00:05:01.346
"Stop. I was just kidding," she said.

90
00:05:01.366 --> 00:05:04.408
"I'll sell you lemonade for fifty cents per cup."

91
00:05:05.489 --> 00:05:07.691
When the boys kept walking, she tried again.

92
00:05:07.711 --> 00:05:09.732
"Okay, okay!

93
00:05:09.793 --> 00:05:10.853
Twenty cents.

94
00:05:11.354 --> 00:05:14.917
That's my special price for cousins and friends of cousins."

95
00:05:14.937 --> 00:05:18.559
"You have a deal," Cole said, turning around.

96
00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.543
Henry and Cole headed back to the lemonade stand.

97
00:05:23.543 --> 00:05:25.565
Maggie poured them each a cup of lemonade.

98
00:05:26.166 --> 00:05:28.948
Henry fished some change out of his pocket to pay for it.

99
00:05:30.188 --> 00:05:30.989
Cole took a sip.

100
00:05:31.009 --> 00:05:33.732
"Hey, this lemonade is really good!"

101
00:05:34.472 --> 00:05:35.413
Maggie smiled.

102
00:05:35.433 --> 00:05:38.876
"It's the best in town," she bragged.

103
00:05:39.877 --> 00:05:41.239
"Everyone says so.

104
00:05:42.099 --> 00:05:43.981
I've made a ton of money already!"

105
00:05:44.942 --> 00:05:48.425
She opened the cashbox on her table to put the boys' money away.

106
00:05:48.926 --> 00:05:51.668
When she looked inside the box, she gasped.

107
00:05:51.688 --> 00:05:53.070
"Oh no!"

108
00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:54.211
she cried.
